<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nayaks of Kandy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1739">1739</a>–<a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaks</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a> were the last royal dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, ruling the Kingdom of Kandy from 1739 to 1815. Of south Indian origin and related by marriage to the Nayak rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, they came to the throne when the last Sinhalese king died without a son, and became patrons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. The last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-vikrama-rajasinha">Sri Vikrama Rajasinha</a>, was deposed by the British.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nayaks-of-kandy.jpg" alt="Nayaks of Kandy" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: McKay Savage from Chennai, India · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sri_Lanka_-_029_-_Kandy_Temple_of_the_Tooth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
